34238 1079 #uuid "e3cf30e8-57fc-566e-adbd-a352b278b915" 13194139534725 17592186045417 true] [17592186434239 1068 #edb/ref 17592186434237 13194139534725 17592186045417 true] [17592186434239 1069 "q-277196" 13194139534725 17592186045417 true] [17592186434239 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534725 17592186045417 true] [17592186434239 1071 "![](images/0a/0ace4ffe981358bf61da04caaaed2c24113e287e22f7c31833bfd68b47218055.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?\n\n{{field-1}}$=1$" 13194139534725 17592186045417 true] [17592186434239 1072 #uuid "6d887ce5-d0d0-5930-95c7-a392e53a9d69" 13194139534725 17592186045417 true] [17592186434239 1074 "Remember that the general equation of an ellipse centered at $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the ellipse is centered at $(3,2),$ the horizontal radius has length $a=4,$ and the vertical radius has length $b=2.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{{4}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{{2}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{16}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{4} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534725 17592186045417 true] [17592186434240 1068 #edb/ref 17592186434238 13194139534725 17592186045417 true] [17592186434240 1069 "q-72250" 13194139534725 17592186045417 true] [17592186434240 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534725 17592186045417 true] [17592186434240 1071 "![](images/d7/d7f6205559fb8b750cdaf121111065cde50adb0afceb90d8d6f4a42305bfdcd4.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?" 13194139534725 17592186045417 true] [17592186434240 1072 #uuid "b4857db7-a62d-50eb-acc9-cbd3a910fcdf" 13194139534725 17592186045417 true] [17592186434240 1074 "Remember that the general equation of an ellipse centered at $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the ellipse is centered at $(-3,2),$ the horizontal radius has length $a=4,$ and the vertical radius has length $b=3.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-(-3))^{2}}{{4}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{{3}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x+3)^{2}}{16}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{9} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534725 17592186045417 true] [17592186434241 1068 #edb/ref 17592186434236 13194139534725 17592186045417 true] [17592186434241 1069 "q-278311" 13194139534725 17592186045417 true] [17592186434241 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534725 17592186045417 true] [17592186434241 1071 "![](images/58/58be29819a83484e2a524e33c27dc2d890dfc722c28d787afded5bc811f898d8.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?\n\n{{field-1}}$=1$" 13194139534725 17592186045417 true] [17592186434241 1072 #uuid "cbea84fd-26bf-5e7a-8622-63b89ac36fbc" 13194139534725 17592186045417 true] [17592186434241 1074 "Remember that the general equation of an ellipse centered at $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the ellipse is centered at $(-2,2),$ the horizontal radius has length $a=5,$ and the vertical radius has length $b=2.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-(-2))^{2}}{{5}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{{2}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x+2)^{2}}{25}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{4} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534725 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-01b3651c-c733-5b49-a154-345b8d98a0ea" 17592186434229 "answer-18c7aee9-61e5-5197-a354-15d93dc615cf" 17592186434230 "answer-926e8795-0fcb-5eea-8386-a90864fab8ab" 17592186434231 "answer-b169ab72-71e1-57f7-b127-19d4b9034ed7" 1759218643423